A bare `:label` keyword with a space-separated name is the plain keyword
in the wrong case: keyword_uppercase, not label_keyword_form (catalog
hand-off). The literal target then matches no label text, since the
stored text starts with the lowercase keyword.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Rewind;
	:DECLARE nTimes;
	nTimes := 0;
	:label START;
	nTimes := nTimes + 1;
	:IF nTimes < 2;
		Branch("LABEL START");
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN nTimes;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Rewind;
	:DECLARE nTimes;
	nTimes := 0;
	:LABEL START;
	nTimes := nTimes + 1;
	:IF nTimes < 2;
		Branch("LABEL START");
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN nTimes;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:2-4:8 warning deprecated_keyword: ':LABEL' is legacy flow control used with Branch(); prefer structured control flow in new code
4:2-4:8 error keyword_uppercase: SSL keywords are case-sensitive and must be uppercase: use ':LABEL'
7:10-7:23 error branch_target_label: Branch target "LABEL START" matches no ':LABEL' in this procedure; the target must equal the label text exactly, keyword included
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
